    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Forgive me for the brief detour into goblin lore. Now, let's dive back into the physics.\n\nThe \"spooky action at a distance\" refers to the phenomenon where entangled particles can instantaneously affect each other, regardless of the distance between them. This seems to defy classical notions of space and time, as it implies that information can be transmitted between particles faster than the speed of light.\n\nEinstein's criticism of entanglement was rooted in his theory of special relativity, which states that nothing can travel faster than the speed of light. He believed that the instantaneous correlation between entangled particles was a form of \"spooky action\" that violated this fundamental principle.\n\nHowever, the key to understanding entanglement lies in the concept of wave function collapse. When two particles are entangled, their wave functions become correlated in such a way that measuring one particle instantly affects the state of the other, regardless of the distance between them.\n\nThink of it like a game of \"ping-pong\" between the particles. When a measurement is made on one particle, it \"bounces\" the wave function of the other particle, causing it to collapse into a specific state. This process happens instantaneously, regardless of the distance between the",
